    "path": "sources/treasury-mts/mts-202605.pdf",
    "table": "Table 5. Outlays of the U.S. Government, May 2026 and Other Periods",
    "page": 20,
    "title": "Social Security Administration section (Table-5 cap-fit unit, page 20). Full 9-column outlays model. Reclassified from over-cap to cap-fit by the 2026-07-15 sizing pass (81 cells, not the earlier 443 which had merged SSA with Independent Agencies). NESTED (family 3): the two Off-Budget trust funds (Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance; Federal Disability Insurance) each roll Benefit Payments + Administrative Expenses into a Total-- row, which then feeds the department roll-up. Family pattern: plans/treasury-mts-2026-05-outlays-table5.md; worked examples: -state (nesting), -legislative.",
    "period": "May FY2026 (This Month = May 2026; Current FYTD = Oct 2025 - May 2026; Prior FYTD = Oct 2024 - May 2025)"
  },
  "unit_note": "USD millions ('[$ millions]' per table header). Table 5 legend (p. 23): '......' = 'No Transactions' (omitted); '(**)' = 'Less than absolute value of $500,000' (none occur in this section). Values as printed, thousands separators stripped, negatives as leading '-'. Nine-column model: 3 periods x (Gross Outlays / Applicable Receipts / Outlays[net]). Off-Budget trust-fund totals nest (family 3). The Proprietary Receipts line is split On-Budget / Off-Budget (two lines), so the Applicable column rolls up with two sources -- no single-source standalone is needed here. The 'Intrabudgetary Transactions / Off-Budget' row carries source footnote 3 ('Includes FICA and SECA tax credits, non-contributory military service credits, special benefits for the aged and credit for the unnegotiated OASI benefit checks.') -- a label annotation, not a value modifier; the value -33 is render-verified clean. Non-default tolerances quote the Table-5 rounding note (p. 23): 'Note: Details may not add to totals due to rounding.'",
